  "query_preview": "../Thursday through Sunday/... Benign days are ahead \ncompared to the last week of strong systems for the panhandle. \nFriday sees the low pressure currently in the northern gulf finally \nfill completely, with another system moving up from the southwest. \nNot expecting this system to reach the southern panhandle fully, \nonly expecting the extreme southern portion to be clipped by some \nmoisture Saturday going into Sunday.\nOtherwise, expect to start out with mostly a cool trend, with \novernight temperatures dipping down into the low to mid 30s, and the \nnorthern panhandle possibly getting down into the upper 20s.\nCould see some northerly winds increase out of Lynn Canal, but \nuncertainty in low strength and has lead to less winds for now.",
